    <h2>What this page could not verify<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <div class="warn">
      Four things, stated plainly so you know which parts of this page are reads and which are reconstruction.
      <br><br>
      <b>1. The digits 325 on the mug.</b> The digits themselves are solid — read twice at high zoom, both passes 3-2-5. What is missing is a lock: no keypad, dial bank or number panel appears anywhere in the footage we sampled, so we will not tell you to type 325 into something. It is a lead for later in the chapter, not a Kitchen code.
      <br><br>
      <b>2. The breaker meter reading.</b> The electricity meter beside the switch row has an LCD readout that three separate passes read three different ways (0000145, 0000345, and 00001.1). At this resolution the digits are not dependable, so no meter number appears on this page. The switch labels are a different matter — C5, C6, S2, H7, M3, T5, E2, P4 were stable across two reads — and those are what the room actually uses.
      <br><br>
      <b>3. The stove / H7 step.</b> The pop-up at 0:46 is legible, and it names H7. We never see the stove being switched off in one clean shot, so the exact step — which switch turns the stove off, and whether H7 is that switch — is the game's hint rather than something we watched happen.
      <br><br>
      <b>4. The ending and the reward.</b> The clip is 3:43 long, but our sampled copy cut out around 3:20, before any results card, exit animation or coin reward. This page therefore prints no reward figure for Kitchen. If you finish the room yourself, the results card is the thing to check.
    </div>
